      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5b4d99a9-d775-5483-b896-d18fa4fbd083",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nivek Ogre, Frank Sinatra, Kevin Crompton, cEvin Key, Dave Ogilvie, Rave, Martin Atkins, George Axelrod, John Frankenheimer, Richard Condon, Laurence Harvey, Janet Leigh, Angela Lansbury, Henry Silva, James Gregory\n- Organizations: Skinny Puppy, Invisible Records\n- Projects: Rx\n- Products: The Voice of Frank Sinatra, From Here to Eternity, The Manchurian Candidate\n- Concepts: industrial music\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Sinatra was born on December 12, 1915, and became an American singer, actor, and producer who was one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\n- Frank Sinatra released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\n- The 1962 film The Manchurian Candidate was adapted by George Axelrod from Richard Condon's 1959 novel, produced by Axelrod and John Frankenheimer, directed by Frankenheimer, and starred Frank Sinatra, Laurence Harvey, and Janet Leigh.\n- Nivek Ogre was born Kevin Graham Ogilvie on December 5, 1962, and is a Canadian musician, performance artist, and actor best known as a founding member of Skinny Puppy.\n- Frank Sinatra's career was revived in 1953 by the success of From Here to Eternity, and that performance won him the Academy Award and Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\n- In Skinny Puppy, Nivek Ogre used his alias partly to distinguish himself from fellow member Kevin Crompton, also known as cEvin Key, and producer Dave Ogilvie, also known as Rave.\n- Rx was a one-off side project by Skinny Puppy member Nivek Ogre in collaboration with Invisible Records founder Martin Atkins.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "af0a80b6-c738-51f5-8359-2c87571e5b54",
        "text": "Page: Nivek Ogre. Sentence: Nivek Ogre (born Kevin Graham Ogilvie December 5, 1962) is a Canadian musician, performance artist and actor best known as a founding member of the industrial music group Skinny Puppy.\nPage: Nivek Ogre. Sentence: Since that band featured another Kevin (Crompton, a.k.a. cEvin Key) and was produced by another Ogilvie (Dave, a.k.a. Rave), Ogre's alias was practical as well as theatrical.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: Francis Albert Sinatra ( ; ] ; December 12, 1915 – May 14, 1998) was an American singer, actor, and producer who was one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: He released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\nPage: Frank Sinatra. Sentence: His career was reborn in 1953 with the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", with his performance subsequently winning an Academy Award and Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\nPage: Rx (band). Sentence: ℞ or Rx was a one-off side project by Skinny Puppy band member Nivek Ogre, in collaboration with Invisible Records founder Martin Atkins.\nPage: The Manchurian Candidate (1962 film). Sentence: The Manchurian Candidate is a 1962 American black and white neo-noir Cold War suspense thriller film scripted by George Axelrod, from the 1959 Richard Condon novel \"The Manchurian Candidate\", produced by Axelrod and John Frankenheimer, directed by Frankenheimer, and starring Frank Sinatra, Laurence Harvey, and Janet Leigh; co-starring are Angela Lansbury, Henry Silva, and James Gregory.",
